    "last_reason": "stop",
    "final_answer": "Upgraded `payout_sync.py` from v1 to the v2 export API and verified it against the live v2 server.\n\n### Changes\n- Uses `GET /v2/payouts` instead of `/v1/payouts`.\n- Follows the opaque `cursor` through every window until `drained: true` \u2014 it does not guess completion from window size.\n- Deduplicates on payout `id`, since v2 windows overlap at their edges.\n- On `429`, reads `Retry-After`, waits, and resends the identical request.\n- On `400 invalid_cursor`, restarts the export without a cursor; the accumulated ID set prevents duplicates.\n- Keeps payout creation order in the output.\n\n### Verification\nAgainst `http://the VM's public address:18080`:\n\n- v2 sync produced **2,431** payouts\n- All 2,431 IDs were unique\n- Result exactly matched the full v1 payout list (same order and content)\n- Mock tests confirmed cursor pagination, edge-overlap deduplication, `Retry-After` handling, and invalid-cursor recovery",
